      "message": "Hi Aiugo!\n\nCould you please clarify on this: the `mPosition` has `uint32_t` type (see below). So when you are applying a 64-bit mask to it, the mask has to be truncated to fit 32-bits. Which 32-bit mask are you aiming to obtain? Maybe it can be expressed directly using 32-bit constants?\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/media/libaudioclient/include/media/AudioTimestamp.h;l\u003d33;drc\u003d5c68943239be52a3bb6d435239500b4c747a490a\n\n```c++\nclass AudioTimestamp {\npublic:\n...\n    uint32_t        mPosition; // a frame position in AudioTrack::getPosition() units\n...\n};\n```",
